# The ports tree commit every build VM checks out.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. poudriere validates a seeded package against the
# EXACT versions its dependencies were recorded with. The published repo is
# built incrementally over many rounds, so the moment the ports tree moves
# under it, every already-published package that pins an older version of a
# rebuilt dependency is discarded from the seed -- and the discard cascades
# down the dependency graph.
#
# That is not theory. On 2026-09-09 the freebsd-builder v2.2.7 release
# changed the prepared-image cache key (freebsd-15.1-2.2.6-... ->
# freebsd-15.1-2.2.7-...), the image was re-prepared, and 'poudriere ports
# -c' cloned the tree afresh at 8d8fa3ed instead of the 742e58ff every one
# of the 26,893 published packages had been built against. expat went
# 2.8.3 -> 2.8.4 in that window, which deleted python312-3.12.14 from the
# seed, which deleted 96 more packages including llvm19, which re-blocked
# 1,744 ports. One round of 18 jobs x 5 hours netted 3 packages.
#
# So the tree is pinned here, the pin is part of the prepare text (and thus
# of the image cache key), and vm_prepare.sh fails the job rather than
# build against a different tree. Moving the pin is a deliberate act that
# costs a rebuild wave -- do it when the tree is otherwise complete, not
# as a side effect of a release somewhere else.
